        "source_file_sha": "c6a7a85dafbe2a6c7ded124859fbd07c8d6de27b",
        "lead_summary": "Crude went down and the sector went up, and the reason is in the product, not the barrel. WTI slipped to $91.11 (-$1.30) and the G-7 agreed on Friday to release 100 million barrels \u2014 with diesel front-loaded in the first twenty days, because diesel is the shortage. Refiners took back everything last week's diplomacy cost them: MPC +7.3% to within a dollar of its record, VLO +4.9%, PSX +3.5%. XLE closed $62.82 (+1.3%) after Tuesday's $60.95 low undercut the 50-day and reversed \u2014 still under the $63.46 breakout line, so the failed breakout stands, but the breakdown did not follow. SLB (-5.4%) is the dissent. OPEC+ meets tomorrow, after this page is written.",
